<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bank of Saint George</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1407–<a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Bank of San Giorgio, Casa di San Giorgio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bank of Saint George, or Casa di San Giorgio, was a financial institution of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, founded in 1407 to consolidate and manage the state's public debt. It collected the taxes assigned to its creditors and in the 15th century took over the administration of Genoese colonies such as Famagusta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Caffa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a>. One of the oldest banks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, it was wound up in 1805.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bank-of-saint-george.jpg" alt="Bank of Saint George" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jensens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palazzo_San_Georgio_Genova_W.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
